Title:
klist2ccache (with klistremote and klistwinrm)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This repo provides Python tooling to convert Windows `klist tgt` output into MIT Kerberos ccache files usable by Impacket and other Linux Kerberos tooling.  
- It includes `klist2ccache.py` for local conversion, plus `klistremote.py` (Task Scheduler + SMB) and `klistwinrm.py` (WinRM) to list/dump Kerberos TGTs from remote Windows hosts without an interactive shell.  
- The tools parse ticket metadata (client/server, key type, flags, validity/renewal times) and write ccaches, with options to dump specific logon sessions and include machine accounts (`--computer`).  
- A key design point is correct handling of Credential Guard: when enabled, `klist` exposes a `KerberosKeyWithMetadata` blob with wrapped key material protected in VTL1, so the tools detect this and refuse to emit unusable ccaches (avoiding `KRB_AP_ERR_BAD_INTEGRITY`).  
- Useful for red teams/pentesters doing Kerberos-based lateral movement with existing access, and for defenders validating Credential Guard’s impact on ticket extraction workflows.

Technical Focus:
- Windows `klist` TGT dumping and parsing
- Kerberos ccache generation (MIT/Heimdal-compatible)
- Remote execution via Task Scheduler + SMB and via WinRM
- Logon session enumeration and ticket selection (including machine accounts)
- Credential Guard / VTL1 protected Kerberos session keys (`KerberosKeyWithMetadata`)
- Impacket Kerberos authentication workflows (`-k -no-pass`, `KRB5CCNAME`)

Use Cases:
- Convert on-host `klist tgt` output into a reusable ccache for Impacket tooling
- Remotely enumerate Kerberos sessions on a Windows target and dump available TGTs
- Perform Kerberos-authenticated lateral movement from Linux using extracted ccaches
- Dump tickets without writing files to disk using SMB named-pipe streaming (`-named-pipes`)
- Validate/assess Credential Guard preventing offline recovery of TGT session keys

Keywords:
Kerberos, TGT, klist, ccache, Impacket, KRB5CCNAME, Windows logon session, LSA, Credential Guard, VTL1, secure kernel, KerberosKeyWithMetadata, WinRM, SMB, Task Scheduler, pass-the-hash, NTLM, AES key, keytab, KRB_AP_ERR_BAD_INTEGRITY